Counts, matched populations and unrounded ratios by reporting unit (CSV)
Population API download (JSON)
Country metadata used to exclude World Bank regional aggregates
Retrieval URLs and source hashes

The comparison uses receiving-country population, not the population of each applicant’s country of origin. Rates are descriptive activity indicators, not measures of the proportion of residents who claimed asylum. Coverage, procedures, repeat applications, and changes in reporting units still matter. World Bank country/economy codes are matched exactly to receiving-country codes; unmatched historical or special codes remain unavailable rather than being reassigned.
These international activity measures include all reported procedural stages. The UK official-statistics comparison deliberately uses a narrower first-instance scope, so its counts can differ.

Choose a receiving country from the dropdown. You can type while the dropdown is focused to jump to a country. Reported applications and decisions combine persons and cases without conversion; they are not counts of unique people. A case can include more than one person, and reporting-unit mixes can vary between countries and years. The chart updates in your browser.
data = FileAttachment("data/explorer.json").json()
formatting = import((await FileAttachment("assets/grant-rates.js").url()) + "?v=grant-rates-rounded-3")
core = import((await FileAttachment("assets/explorer-core.js").url()) + "?v=combined-units-2")
{
  const p = document.createElement("p");
  p.className = "reading-note";
  const m = data.metadata;
