}






Blue line and dots: applications. Stacked bars: recorded decision outcomes. Hover over a dot or bar for its value. Decisions can relate to applications made in earlier years. A gap means no value is available in the stored source data, not a confirmed zero.

How are decisions recorded?

{
  const complete = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.decisions &gt; 0 &&
    core.outcomes.every(([key]) =&gt; d[key] != null) &&
    core.outcomes.reduce((sum, [key]) =&gt; sum + d[key], 0) === d.decisions);
  if (!complete.length) {
    const p = document.createElement("p");
    p.textContent = "No complete positive decision totals are available for an outcome-share chart.";
    return p;
  }
  const shares = complete.flatMap(d =&gt; core.outcomes.map(([key, outcome]) =&gt; ({
    year: d.year, share: d[key] / d.decisions, outcome, count: d[key]
  })));
  return Plot.plot({
    width: Math.min(width, 1100), height: 350, marginLeft: 75,
    style: {background: "white", color: "#20383b", fontFamily: "Segoe UI, sans-serif", fontSize: "13px"},
    ariaLabel: "Annual decision-outcome shares for " + selected.name,
    x: {type: "band", label: "Year", tickFormat: d =&gt; d % 5 === 0 || d === data.metadata.year_to_available ? String(d) : ""},
    y: {domain: [0, 1], tickFormat: d =&gt; Math.round(d * 100) + "%", label: "Share of recorded decisions", grid: true},
    color: {domain: core.outcomes.map(d =&gt; d[1]), range: core.outcomes.map(d =&gt; d[2])},
    marks: [Plot.barY(shares, Plot.stackY({
      x: "year", y: "share", fill: "outcome",
      title: d =&gt; d.year + " · " + d.outcome + ": " + formatting.percent(d.share) + " (" + d.count.toLocaleString("en-GB") + ")"
    })), Plot.ruleY([0])]
  });
}






These are annual outcome shares, including administrative closures in the denominator—not cohort success probabilities or substantive-decision recognition rates. Years without a complete, positive, reconciled outcome total are omitted from this percentage chart. Definitions and limitations.
About the country commentary. The gallery profiles describe the fixed 2000-2025 UNHCR extract, not a forecast. Changes compare reported application activity with 2019 where available; peaks are the largest recorded annual totals. Grant rates exclude closures and use complete, positive, reconciled decision totals; they concern decisions made, not outcomes for that year’s arrivals. Procedures, persons/cases mixes and coverage can change. Missing observations remain unavailable rather than being filled with zero. The Grant Rates page separately identifies its refreshed snapshot. Methods and definitions.

Source links and downloads

{
