Grants and refusals, excluding closures
Here the denominator is substantive decisions: refugee status + other protection + rejection. It is not applications received, and it excludes “otherwise closed” outcomes. Applications in one year are not necessarily decided in that year. Closures remain visible in their own comparisons below.

{
  const panel=document.createElement("div");
  const definitions=[["recognised","Refugee status","#00a98f"],["other_protection","Other protection","#f4c542"],["rejected","Refused","#ef6655"]];
  const denominator=total.recognised+total.other_protection+total.rejected;
  if (!total.valid || !(denominator&gt;0)) {panel.textContent="No eligible substantive decisions are available for this selection.";return panel;}
  const headline=document.createElement("p");headline.className="explorer-status";
  headline.textContent=selected.name+" · Overall eligible period: "+definitions.map(([key,label])=&gt;label+" "+percent(total[key]/denominator)).join(" · ")+" · Substantive decisions: "+denominator.toLocaleString("en-GB")+". Closures excluded from these percentages: "+total.closed.toLocaleString("en-GB")+".";
  const values=rows.filter(d=&gt;d.valid && d.recognised+d.other_protection+d.rejected&gt;0).flatMap(d=&gt;definitions.map(([key,label])=&gt;({year:d.year,outcome:label,value:d[key]/(d.recognised+d.other_protection+d.rejected),count:d[key],denominator:d.recognised+d.other_protection+d.rejected})));
  panel.append(headline,Plot.plot({
    width:Math.min(width,1100),height:340,marginLeft:70,
    ariaLabel:"Substantive decision outcomes excluding closures for "+selected.name,
    x:{type:"band",domain:rows.map(d=&gt;d.year),label:"Year",tickFormat:d=&gt;d%5===0||d===data.metadata.year_to_available?String(d):""},
    y:{domain:[0,1],label:"Share of substantive decisions",grid:true,tickFormat:d=&gt;Math.round(d*100)+"%"},
    color:{domain:definitions.map(d=&gt;d[1]),range:definitions.map(d=&gt;d[2]),legend:true},
    marks:[Plot.barY(values,Plot.stackY({x:"year",y:"value",fill:"outcome",title:d=&gt;d.year+" · "+d.outcome+": "+percent(d.value)+" ("+d.count.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" / "+d.denominator.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" substantive decisions)"}))]
  }));
  return panel;
}






Overall percentages divide the summed outcomes by the summed substantive decisions across eligible years. The chart uses the same complete, reconciled country-year records as the grant-rate figures; unavailable years remain gaps. Refugee status and other protection together give the total-protection rate. Refusal is the remaining substantive outcome. Persons and cases remain combined without conversion in this international explorer.
Compare UK official initial-decision statistics with UNHCR.

Where did applicants come from—and who received grants?
The receiving-country dropdown above controls this section. Choose a year to see the country’s annual grant rates and two different Top 3 lists. Origins are ranked by counts, not by the highest percentage: one list shows where reported applications originated, the other where grant recipients originated.

originYearData = FileAttachment("data/origin-year-explorer.json").json()
originCards = import((await FileAttachment("assets/origin-year-cards.js").url()) + "?v=2")
















viewof originYear = Inputs.select(Array.from({length:data.metadata.year_to_available-data.metadata.year_from+1},(_,i)=&gt;data.metadata.year_from+i),{label:"Applications and grants year",value:data.metadata.year_to_available,format:String})
viewof grantDefinition = Inputs.radio(new Map([["Refugee status only","refugee"],["Any protection: refugee status + other protection","protection"]]),{label:"Rank grant recipients by",value:"refugee"})
















{
  const group=originYearData.groups[selected.iso]?.[String(originYear)];
  const panel=document.createElement("div");panel.className="origin-year-selection";
  const title=document.createElement("h3");title.textContent=selected.name+" · "+originYear;
  const summary=document.createElement("p");summary.className="explorer-status origin-year-summary";
  if (!group) summary.textContent="No application or decision records are available for this country and year.";
  else {
    const rate=grants.rates(group.summary);
    const number=value=&gt;value==null?"Unavailable":value.toLocaleString("en-GB");
    summary.textContent="Applications: "+number(group.summary.applications)+" · Decisions: "+number(group.summary.decisions)+" · Refugee recognition rate: "+percent(rate.refugee_rate)+" · Total protection rate: "+percent(rate.protection_rate)+" · Closure share: "+percent(rate.closed_share)+".";
  }
  panel.append(title,summary,originCards.cards(group,originYearData.origins,grantDefinition,grants));return panel;
}






Refugee and total-protection rates use substantive decisions; closure shares use all recorded decisions. Rates are unavailable where outcome counts do not reconcile to a positive decision total. Flags identify the recorded country of origin, not a verification of citizenship; unknown origins have no flag. Applications and grants are different annual flows: recipients may have applied in earlier years. Persons and cases are combined without conversion, and ranks do not estimate an individual’s chance of success. Ties are resolved by origin code.
This section uses the exact source ZIP behind the country explorer, with independently checked country-year totals. Its year selection is separate from the closure-comparison year below.
Flag artwork is bundled locally from FlagCDN; names and ISO codes remain visible alongside each flag.

Closures: changes over time and differences between countries
Closure share = otherwise-closed decisions ÷ all recorded decisions. Closures are processing outcomes without a substantive grant or refusal. They deserve a separate view from recognition rates.
UNHCR’s “otherwise closed” category can include withdrawal and abandonment, but also inadmissibility, death, or transfers under European procedures. It does not identify how many claimants abandoned a claim while remaining in-country. Differences can reflect procedure and reporting as well as claimant behaviour. UNHCR reporting definitions.

The selected country’s closure trend
The country dropdown above controls this chart. The scale is fixed at 0–100% so different countries remain comparable. Hover for the percentage, closure count, and decision denominator.

{
  const valid = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.valid);
  const panel = document.createElement("div");
  if (!valid.length) { panel.textContent = "No complete decision totals are available for this country's closure trend."; return panel; }
  const first = valid[0], latest = valid[valid.length-1];
  const difference = (latest.closed_share-first.closed_share)*100;
  const note = document.createElement("p"); note.className="explorer-status";
  note.textContent = selected.name + ": " + percent(latest.closed_share) + " in " + latest.year +
    " (" + latest.closed.toLocaleString("en-GB") + " closures / " + latest.decisions.toLocaleString("en-GB") +
    " recorded decisions). Change since " + first.year + ": " + (difference&gt;0?"+":"") + difference.toFixed(1) + " percentage points. Overall eligible-period share: " + percent(total.closed_share) + ".";
  panel.append(note,Plot.plot({
    width:Math.min(width,1100),height:330,marginLeft:70,
    ariaLabel:"Closure share over time for "+selected.name,
    x:{label:"Year",ticks:rows.filter(d=&gt;d.year%5===0||d.year===data.metadata.year_to_available).map(d=&gt;d.year),tickFormat:String},
    y:{domain:[0,1],label:"Closures / all recorded decisions",tickFormat:d=&gt;Math.round(d*100)+"%",grid:true},
    marks:[Plot.lineY(rows,{x:"year",y:d=&gt;d.valid?d.closed_share:null,stroke:"#8574bd",strokeWidth:3}),
      Plot.dot(valid,{x:"year",y:"closed_share",fill:"#8574bd",r:4,title:d=&gt;d.year+": "+percent(d.closed_share)+" · "+d.closed.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" closures / "+d.decisions.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" decisions"})]
  }));
  return panel;
}








Top 20 receiving countries: the same year, side by side
Choose a year to compare the same denominator and calendar year across the Top 20 receiving countries. Countries with unavailable or unreconciled totals are omitted from the bars and marked unavailable in the table. Small decision totals can produce volatile percentages; counts are shown in the table and hover labels.

viewof closureYear = Inputs.select(Array.from({length:data.metadata.year_to_available-data.metadata.year_from+1},(_,i)=&gt;data.metadata.year_from+i),{label:"Comparison year",value:data.metadata.year_to_available,format:String})







closureName = country =&gt; ({GBR:"United Kingdom",USA:"United States",TUR:"Türkiye",RUS:"Russia"}[country.iso] || country.name)
closureHistory = topCountries.flatMap(country =&gt; core.countryYears(data,country.iso).map(grants.rates).map(row=&gt;({...row,name:closureName(country)})))
closureComparison = closureHistory.filter(d=&gt;d.year===closureYear).sort((a,b)=&gt;(b.closed_share??-1)-(a.closed_share??-1))























Plot.plot({
  width:Math.min(width,1100),height:620,marginLeft:Math.min(220,width*.32),marginRight:45,
  ariaLabel:"Closure shares across Top 20 receiving countries in "+closureYear,
  x:{domain:[0,1],label:"Closures as a share of all recorded decisions",tickFormat:d=&gt;Math.round(d*100)+"%",grid:true},
  y:{domain:closureComparison.filter(d=&gt;d.valid).map(d=&gt;d.name),label:null},
  marks:[Plot.barX(closureComparison.filter(d=&gt;d.valid),{x:"closed_share",y:"name",fill:"#8574bd",title:d=&gt;d.name+" · "+percent(d.closed_share)+" · "+d.closed.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" closures / "+d.decisions.toLocaleString("en-GB")+" decisions"}),
    Plot.text(closureComparison.filter(d=&gt;d.valid),{x:"closed_share",y:"name",text:d=&gt;percent(d.closed_share),dx:6,textAnchor:"start",fontSize:11})]
})







Inputs.table(closureComparison,{
 columns:["name","closed","decisions","closed_share"],
 header:{name:"Receiving country",closed:"Otherwise closed",decisions:"All decisions",closed_share:"Closure share"},
 format:{closed_share:percent},rows:20
